<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP SEMIFINAL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP SEMIFINAL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South</p>
<p>American Libertadores Cup semifinal, second leg matches played</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>In Lima: Sporting Cristal (Peru) 4 Racing Club (Argentina)</p>
<p>1 (halftime 2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sporting Cristal - Luis Bonnet (5, 55 penalty), Julio</p>
<p>Rivera (42), Nolberto Solano (73)</p>
<p>Racing Club - Marcelo Delgado (35)</p>
<p>Attendance; 45,000</p>
<p>Sporting Cristal win 6-4 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Santiago: Colo Colo (Chile) 3 Cruzeiro (Brazil) 2 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Colo Colo - Ivo Basay (20, 47, 51)</p>
<p>Cruzeiro - Marcelo (29), Cleison (64)</p>
<p>Aggregate score 3-3. Cruzeiro win 5-4 on penalties.</p>
<p>Final to be played over two legs. First leg in Lima on</p>
<p>August 6, second leg in Belo Horizonte, Brazil, on August 13.</p>
</text>
